{
  "about": "The characters a label from the node may hold that reorder or hide how a line reads, as the node's `is_hidden_char` (crates/agency-proto/src/org.rs) has them: every one is printed as `mark`. Ranges are inclusive code points in hex. The set is the controls (Cc), the line and paragraph separators (U+2028, U+2029), the bidirectional controls, and the format characters (Cf) that are invisible or change how a line is laid out: the soft hyphen, the Mongolian vowel separator, the word joiner and the invisible operators and deprecated format characters up to U+206F, the interlinear annotation marks, the byte-order mark and the language tag. U+200C, U+200D, the emoji tag characters and the format characters that belong to a script's own text (Arabic, Syriac and Kaithi number and end-of-verse signs, the Egyptian hieroglyph, shorthand and musical format controls) are not in it. Swift, the web client and the node read this one file. A text an agent or a person wrote with lines (a context, a document, a thread message, a decision's text) hides exactly `hidden` minus `textKeeps` (a tab, a line feed, a carriage return stay: they cannot reorder a line); `textCases` are such texts and what each prints as. Labels and titles use `cases`.",
